# Database rules

## MySQL everywhere

Target MySQL 8+ / MariaDB 10.6+ in development, tests and CI, because production is shared hosting. Do not introduce PostgreSQL-only or SQLite-only behaviour.

## Provider settings live in JSON, stable attributes in columns

Provider-specific settings belong in a JSON `config` column. Never add provider-specific columns such as `rss_url`, `subreddit` or `html_selector` to shared tables. Attributes the application filters, sorts or joins on stay real columns.

## Idempotency is enforced by the schema

Content items are unique per source plus external id, falling back to source plus canonical URL. Deliveries are unique per content item, broadcast and destination. A repeated run must never produce a duplicate publish.
